PLOS multi-state analysis code
This repository contains R code accompanying a PLOS Medicine article using multi-state modelling to estimate transition hazards and state occupation probabilities.
Repository contents
PLOS_multi_state/
├── README.md
├── R/
│   ├── 00_transition_matrix.R
│   ├── 01_main_model_fitting.Rmd
│   ├── 02_predict_state_occupation_probabilities.R
│   ├── 03_plot_state_occupation_probabilities.R
│   ├── 04_plot_cvr_contrasts.R
│   └── functions/
│       ├── load_fitted_models.R
│       ├── occurrence_probability_difference.R
│       └── transition_matrix.R
├── results/
│   └── README.md
├── figures/
│   └── README.md
└── renv.lock or session_info.txt
Suggested workflow
Run the scripts in the following order:
R/01_main_model_fitting.Rmd — prepares the multi-state dataset, selects spline complexity, fits transition-specific flexible parametric survival models, and saves fitted model objects.
R/02_predict_state_occupation_probabilities.R — loads the fitted models and generates predicted 10-year state occupation probabilities by baseline age group.
R/03_plot_state_occupation_probabilities.R — creates state occupation probability plots corresponding to the main manuscript figures.
R/04_plot_cvr_contrasts.R — creates contrast plots for cardiovascular/renal event probabilities.
